From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Judd <ipajudd@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:15:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the Trader scoring every Megalomaniac as no change

TradeQuery:GetResultEvaluation weighs a Megalomaniac by adding its notables
with calcFunc({ addNodes = ... }). It looks each one up in tree.notableMap
and keeps only a node whose `recipes` field is set. The tree gives a notable
a `recipe` field, so no node passed the check, nothing was added, and every
Megalomaniac listing scored the same as the build without it.

Check `recipe`, the field the tree sets.
---
 src/Classes/TradeQuery.lua | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Classes/TradeQuery.lua b/src/Classes/TradeQuery.lua
index bf67e9c..7b158d0 100644
--- a/src/Classes/TradeQuery.lua
+++ b/src/Classes/TradeQuery.lua
@@ -909,7 +909,7 @@ function TradeQueryClass:GetResultEvaluation(row_idx, result_index, calcFunc, ba
 		local addedNodes = {}
 		for nodeName in (result.item_string.."\r\n"):gmatch("Allocates (.-)\r?\n") do
 			local node = self.itemsTab.build.spec.tree.notableMap[nodeName:lower()]
-			if node and node.recipes ~= nil then
+			if node and node.recipe ~= nil then
 				addedNodes[node] = true
 			end
 		end
